    {
        "content": "<p>Hi,</p>\n<p>to prepare myself for AoC, I try to understand the parser package again. I have to relearn the concept every year, so I want to give me a bit of a head start.</p>\n<p>I have this code: </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"CoffeeScript\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"nv\">parse_line</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Parser</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">List</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">U8</span><span class=\"p\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"nx\">Left</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">U64</span><span class=\"p\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Right</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">U64</span><span class=\"p\">)],</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">_</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"nv\">parse_line</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nx\">Parser</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">one_of</span><span class=\"p\">([</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"nx\">parse_left</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"nx\">parse_right</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">])</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"nv\">parse_left</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Parser</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">List</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">U8</span><span class=\"p\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"nx\">Left</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">U64</span><span class=\"p\">)],</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">_</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"nv\">parse_left</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nx\">Parser</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">const</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"o\">|</span><span class=\"nx\">n</span><span class=\"o\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Left</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">n</span><span class=\"p\">)).</span><span class=\"nx\">skip</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">Parser</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">Utf8</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">codeunit</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">'L'</span><span class=\"p\">)).</span><span class=\"nx\">keep</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">Parser</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">Utf8</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">digits</span><span class=\"p\">({}))</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"nv\">parse_right</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Parser</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">List</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">U8</span><span class=\"p\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"nx\">Right</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">U64</span><span class=\"p\">)],</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">_</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"nv\">parse_right</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nx\">Parser</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">const</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"o\">|</span><span class=\"nx\">n</span><span class=\"o\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Right</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">n</span><span class=\"p\">)).</span><span class=\"nx\">skip</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">Parser</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">Utf8</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">codeunit</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">'R'</span><span class=\"p\">)).</span><span class=\"nx\">keep</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">Parser</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">Utf8</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">digits</span><span class=\"p\">({}))</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>It fails with the message:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\"><pre><span></span><code>── ✗ type mismatch ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nThe two elements in this list have incompatible types.\n\nparse_right,\n^^^^^^^^^^^\n\nThe first element has this type:\n\n    Parser(List(U8), [Left(U64)], [ExpectedByte(U8), ExpectedBytes(List(U8)), ExpectedDigit, ExpectedPredicate, IntegerOverflow(U64),\n    InvalidUtf8, UnexpectedEnd])\n\nHowever, the second element has this type:\n\n    Parser(List(U8), [Right(U64)], [ExpectedByte(U8), ExpectedBytes(List(U8)), ExpectedDigit, ExpectedPredicate, IntegerOverflow(U64),\n    InvalidUtf8, UnexpectedEnd])\n\nAll elements in a list must have compatible types.\nNote: You can wrap each element in a tag to make them compatible.\nTo learn about tags, see &lt;https://www.roc-lang.org/tutorial#tags&gt;\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>It works, if I remove the type annotation of <code>parse_left</code> and <code>parse_right</code>, since then the type gets inferred to have <code>[Left(U64) ,Right(U64)]</code></p>\n<p>I tried to \"open\" the type by adding <code>..</code>: <code>parse_left : Parser(List(U8), [Left(U64), ..], _)</code>. But this gets the error:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\"><pre><span></span><code>── ✗ value is not polymorphic ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nThe type annotation on parse_left says it can be used at many types, but parse_left isn't defined as a function (like |x| ...), so it can only\nhave one type.\n\nparse_left : Parser(List(U8), [Left(U64), ..], _)\n^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n\nIf you want me to infer its type, remove each .., or write a concrete type.\n\nIf you want to use it at many types, make it a function that takes {}:\n    parse_left : {} -&gt; Parser(List(U8), [Left(U64), ..], _)\n    parse_left = |{}| ...\nThen call it as parse_left({}) wherever you use it.\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>The hint works:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"CoffeeScript\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"nv\">parse_line</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Parser</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">List</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">U8</span><span class=\"p\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"nx\">Left</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">U64</span><span class=\"p\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Right</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">U64</span><span class=\"p\">)],</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">_</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"nv\">parse_line</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nx\">Parser</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">one_of</span><span class=\"p\">([</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"nx\">parse_left</span><span class=\"p\">(),</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"nx\">parse_right</span><span class=\"p\">(),</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">])</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"nv\">parse_left</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">() -&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Parser</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">List</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">U8</span><span class=\"p\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"nx\">Left</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">U64</span><span class=\"p\">)],</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">_</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"nv\">parse_left</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">||</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nx\">Parser</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">const</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"o\">|</span><span class=\"nx\">n</span><span class=\"o\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Left</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">n</span><span class=\"p\">)).</span><span class=\"nx\">skip</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">Parser</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">Utf8</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">codeunit</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">'L'</span><span class=\"p\">)).</span><span class=\"nx\">keep</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">Parser</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">Utf8</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">digits</span><span class=\"p\">({}))</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"nv\">parse_right</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">() -&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Parser</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">List</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">U8</span><span class=\"p\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"nx\">Right</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">U64</span><span class=\"p\">)],</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">_</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"nv\">parse_right</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">||</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nx\">Parser</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">const</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"o\">|</span><span class=\"nx\">n</span><span class=\"o\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Right</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">n</span><span class=\"p\">)).</span><span class=\"nx\">skip</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">Parser</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">Utf8</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">codeunit</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">'R'</span><span class=\"p\">)).</span><span class=\"nx\">keep</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">Parser</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">Utf8</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">digits</span><span class=\"p\">({}))</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I don't like this solution/workaround. Most of the time, I add the types after the fact, when I debug the code. It is not so nice, that I have to rewrite the parsers as functions, to add types.</p>\n<p>Is there a way to open the type of a parser without writing it as a function?</p>",
